@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@accessToken = replace-with-auth0-access-token
@secondAccessToken = replace-with-second-auth0-access-token
@habitId = replace-with-created-habit-id
@maintenanceKey = moodly-local-maintenance
@cdcEntryId = replace-with-created-entry-id

### Auth0 token note
# Obtain an access token through Auth0 Universal Login in the local SPA, with
# audience={{AUTH0_AUDIENCE}}. Paste user A's token into @accessToken and user B's
# token into @secondAccessToken. Do not use an ID token: the API requires an access token.

### Create a habit
POST {{baseUrl}}/habits
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Exercise",
  "icon": "🏃",
  "targetFrequency": "daily"
}

### List active habits
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Mark a habit as done today
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/entries/today
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "habitId": "{{habitId}}",
  "done": true,
  "note": "30-minute run"
}

### Set today's mood
PUT {{baseUrl}}/entries/today/mood
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "score": 4,
  "tags": ["productive", "tired"],
  "note": "I was tired today because I stayed up late."
}

### Query entries by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get current habit streak
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits/{{habitId}}/streak
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get weekly mood trend
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/mood-trend?period=week
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get most missed habits
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/most-missed-habits
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### CDC verification: inspect listener health and failed-event count
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Search indexed mood notes, habit notes, and mood tags
# Search is eventually consistent: wait briefly after saving the entry.
GET {{baseUrl}}/entries/search?q=tired&from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Cross-user isolation: user B must not see user A's habits or search results
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits
Authorization: Bearer {{secondAccessToken}}

### Invalid/expired/wrong-audience token: each must return 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{baseUrl}}/habits
Authorization: Bearer invalid-or-expired-token

### Avatar: request a short-lived signed upload payload as user A
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar/upload-signature
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contentType": "image/png",
  "sizeBytes": 1024
}

### Avatar: upload directly to the returned uploadUrl
# Send multipart/form-data to data.uploadUrl with file plus data.apiKey,
# data.timestamp, data.signature, data.publicId, and data.uploadPreset. Copy the
# Cloudinary response's public_id and version into the confirm request below.

### Avatar: confirm only the Cloudinary response for the payload above
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "publicId": "replace-with-cloudinary-public_id",
  "version": 1
}

### Avatar: retrieve the persisted metadata and safe delivery URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Avatar ownership: user B cannot confirm user A's Cloudinary public ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/avatar/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{secondAccessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "publicId": "replace-with-user-a-public_id",
  "version": 1
}

### CDC verification: inspect an indexed entry
# Set cdcEntryId at the top from the response to the entry update request.
GET http://localhost:9200/daily_entries_search/_doc/{{cdcEntryId}}

### CDC verification: duplicate-safe full rebuild
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/cdc/reindex
X-Maintenance-Key: {{maintenanceKey}}

### CDC verification: replay one dead-letter after Elasticsearch recovers
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/cdc/dead-letters/replace-with-dead-letter-id/replay
X-Maintenance-Key: {{maintenanceKey}}

### CDC verification: delete (no entry-delete API exists yet)
# Run this in mongosh, then the indexed-entry request above should return 404.
# db.daily_entries.deleteOne({ _id: ObjectId("your-entry-id") })
